Subject: [PATCH] gemini-live: provision API key from NVS in main.c

The Gemini Live touch-to-talk path starts on boot (touch_monitor_task →
cap_gemini_live_toggle), but main.c never handed the capability an API
key, so every BidiGenerateContent WebSocket session opened with no auth
and the session task aborted with "No Gemini API key". The key already
lives in NVS via app_config (struct field `gemini_api_key`, NVS key
"gemini_key") — nothing was reading it into the capability.

Fix: one call inside the existing `#if CONFIG_APP_CLAW_CAP_GEMINI_LIVE`
block in app_main(), immediately before the touch monitor starts:

    cap_gemini_live_set_api_key(s_config->gemini_api_key);

Field access is used directly because app_config exposes NO getter for
this field (the only getter is app_config_get_timezone); `s_config` is
already dereferenced the same way elsewhere (e.g. s_config->wifi_ssid).

Applied to the generated tree by scripts/bootstrap.sh
(apply_gemini_live_api_key_patch), registered in main() right after
apply_gemini_live_main_require_patch. Idempotent: guarded on
grep "cap_gemini_live_set_api_key", anchored on the unique
xTaskCreate(touch_monitor_task, ...) line.

PROVISIONING (how a key gets into NVS):
  - POST /api/config with the JSON field `gemini_api_key` (NVS key
    "gemini_key"), OR a direct NVS write.
  - The dashboard frontend does NOT yet expose a gemini_api_key input
    (only llm_api_key), and there is no `gemini-live` CLI set-key
    subcommand. Adding a frontend field or CLI subcommand is a follow-up
    so a key can be set without a raw NVS write.

NOTE: documentation record of a generated-tree mutation, not a unified
diff against tracked files (same idiom as patches/0009, 0010, 0020). The
mechanism is the python hunk in apply_gemini_live_api_key_patch().
